+Description:
+		The directory name abbreviates "version kernel". It contains
+		immutable metadata describing the running zeroday0619
+		high-performance custom kernel. All attributes are read-only and
+		newline-terminated.
+
+What:		/sys/kernel/v_kernel/kernel_release
+Date:		August 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.2
+Contact:	zeroday0619 high-performance custom kernel maintainers
+Description:
+		The complete kernel release string. For example,
+		"7.2.0-fxsenshi-llvm-v1+".
+
+What:		/sys/kernel/v_kernel/kernel_version
+Date:		August 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.2
+Contact:	zeroday0619 high-performance custom kernel maintainers
+Description:
+		The base Linux version without the custom release metadata. For
+		example,
+		"7.2.0".
+
+What:		/sys/kernel/v_kernel/kernel_codename
+Date:		August 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.2
+Contact:	zeroday0619 high-performance custom kernel maintainers
+Description:
+		The distribution-specific codename configured by
+		CONFIG_V_KERNEL_CODENAME.
+
+What:		/sys/kernel/v_kernel/kernel_buildtype
+Date:		August 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.2
+Contact:	zeroday0619 high-performance custom kernel maintainers
+Description:
+		The compiler family used to build the kernel. The value is "llvm"
+		for Clang builds and "gcc" for GCC builds.
+
+What:		/sys/kernel/v_kernel/kernel_revision
+Date:		August 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.2
+Contact:	zeroday0619 high-performance custom kernel maintainers
+Description:
+		The distribution-specific revision configured by
+		CONFIG_V_KERNEL_REVISION.
+
+What:		/sys/kernel/v_kernel/system_architecture
+Date:		August 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.2
+Contact:	zeroday0619 high-performance custom kernel maintainers
+Description:
+		The target architecture recorded in UTS_MACHINE at build time.
+
+What:		/sys/kernel/v_kernel/build_uuid
+Date:		August 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.2
+Contact:	zeroday0619 high-performance custom kernel maintainers
+Description:
+		A UUIDv8 derived from the GNU build ID of the running vmlinux.
+		Identical vmlinux binaries have identical values. The attribute has
+		mode 0400 because the stable identifier can be used to correlate
+		systems. It is readable only by root and must not be treated as a
+		secret or credential.
